# mtf_cam formal (testplan §3, F-05 / F-06 / K8). Run via `make -C hw/mtf_cam formal`
# (common Makefile.cocotb: FORMAL_SBY defaults to synth/formal.sby; sby is run with cwd = module dir).
#
# Frontend: read_slang (the Yosys slang SystemVerilog frontend). Required because the mtf_list list
# invariants observe internal state (dut.lst, dut.rem_q): the built-in Verilog frontend supports
# neither hierarchical reads nor SystemVerilog `bind`, but slang resolves both correctly. The handshake
# proof is port-only and would work with either frontend; it uses slang here for uniformity.
#
# Tasks:
#   prove       - mtf_list list invariants (i)/(ii)/(iii), N_LIST=16, unbounded k-INDUCTION. K8 core;
#                 this is the COMPLETE proof of the three invariants (unbounded > any bounded check).
#   bmc         - mtf_list permutation at the production width N_LIST=256, bounded BMC (two-probe form,
#                 MOVE_CHK=0/PERM_FULL=0). Reaches depth 6 (the fill's 256-deep priority encoder walls
#                 the unrolling -- see the N_LIST=256 depth note below). Full-generality width check.
#   bmc256moves - N_LIST=256 permutation preservation across >=20 MOVE cycles (PRD-K8 depth target).
#                 Fill-abstracted: the DUT is assumed to START in a valid post-fill state (rem_q==0,
#                 fill done) and re-init is forbidden, so the 256-deep priority encoder that walls `bmc`
#                 at depth 6 is inert and BMC spends its whole depth budget on moves. PASSES at DEPTH 24
#                 (>= PRD-K8's 20). See the honest-scope note below.
#   famoves_cover - non-vacuity witness for bmc256moves: the abstracted move regime is reachable and
#                 non-trivial (filled list, moves incl. back-to-back). Proves the assumes are satisfiable.
#   cover       - mtf_list cover traces (cg_fml), N_LIST=16.
#   hs          - m_l AXIS handshake on mtf_pack (F-06), bounded BMC.
#   hscover     - handshake cover traces.
#
# N_LIST=256 depth -- what is and is NOT proven at the production width (honest scope):
#  * `prove` gives the COMPLETE unbounded proof of all three invariants at N_LIST=16 (k-induction).
#  * `bmc` bounded-checks the full permutation at N_LIST=256 to depth 6. Raising its depth walls: the
#    fill is a 256-deep lowest-set-bit priority-encoder chain (~530 logic levels) and unrolling it is
#    intractable for every engine tried (smtbmc+boolector/yices/z3/bitwuzla, btor btormc, abc bmc3/pdr).
#  * PRD-K8 wants a N_LIST=256 bounded run at depth >= 20. `bmc256moves` reaches it by ABSTRACTING the
#    fill: it assumes a valid post-fill start (rem_q==0, filling done, a valid permutation of the used
#    set) and forbids re-init, which collapses the encoder, then proves move-to-front PRESERVES the
#    permutation for 24 consecutive move cycles. The fill's own correctness is covered by the
#    `n_used==popcount(used&~rem)` assert and by the complete N_LIST=16 induction -- NOT by this task.
#    To keep the SAT problem tractable this task pins the CONCRETE canonical post-fill state
#    used={0..FA_NUSED-1}, lst[i]=i (FA_NUSED=8 live entries; only the moves stay free). Because the RTL
#    move logic is value-agnostic (it shuffles list POSITIONS, never inspects the byte values), the
#    permutation-preservation shown from this one concrete state exercises the full move-shift network.
#    Full-occupancy (up to 256 live) or free-used-set preservation across >20 moves stays SAT-intractable
#    (the solver must brute-force that each 256-wide shift is a bijection over an arbitrary permutation);
#    the harness's general FA_NUSED=0 mode (free used set, ascending-fill pin) confirms the encoder
#    collapse but reaches only a shallow depth, so it is not run in the default flow.
#  * k-INDUCTION at N_LIST=256 (an unbounded proof at production width) was attempted with a free-witness
#    O(N) permutation encoding: its BASECASE passed but the induction did not close within the 15-min
#    time-box (permutation-preservation across the transition is SAT-hard at width 256), so it is not a
#    task here. The bounded bmc256moves depth-24 result is the strongest tractable N_LIST=256 guarantee.

[options]
mode cover
depth 24

[engines]
# boolector bit-blasts (via memory_map above) and closes the O(N^2) permutation logic far faster
# than the default yices on this design (yices stalls on the k-induction query).
smtbmc boolector

# memory_map + opt after prep bit-blasts the list/buffer arrays to registers (slang otherwise keeps
# them as SMT arrays, which makes the O(N^2) permutation logic far slower for smtbmc).
[script]
read_slang mtf_list.sv mtf_list_inv.sv --top mtf_list_inv -G N_LIST=256 -G MOVE_CHK=0 -G PERM_FULL=0 -G PROBE_CHK=1 -G FILL_ABSTRACT=1 -G FA_NUSED=8
prep -top mtf_list_inv
memory_map
opt -fast

[files]
rtl/mtf_list.sv
rtl/mtf_pack.sv
formal/mtf_list_inv.sv
formal/handshake.sv
